{'name': 'Lovin Oven Mediterranean', 'address': '6578 Trigo Rd', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Food, Bakeries, Mediterranean', 'hours': {'Monday': '12:0-21:0', 'Tuesday': '12:0-21:0', 'Wednesday': '12:0-21:0', 'Thursday': '12:0-21:0', 'Friday': '12:0-21:0', 'Saturday': '12:0-21:0', 'Sunday': '12:0-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2015-11-04 04:29:50', 'review_text': "I want to like this place, but it's just too much of a letdown. Their food is good. There aren't a whole lot of Mediterranean places around and this place is a decent price. The problem is, I've tried to come here 4 times and the always seem to be out of rice. The first time I went, they told me there probably wasn't enough left, then they were able to give me some, so I guess I got the bottom of the barrel. The next 3 times they said they were out. What kind of Mediterranean place runs out of rice? It's insane. There's never even anyone there, are they only making enough for like 3 portions? As good as it was the first time, I don't think I'm going to try coming here again"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2015-11-04 01:17:44', 'review_text': "Great food, you order your food and they make it for you, it's not bought or pre made, it's fresh. I love Mediterranean food and finding it in Isla Vista is even better. Make sure to try the cheese bourak and zaatar manaesh! The chicken shawerma is also very good :)"}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2015-10-13 20:21:15', 'review_text': "I had passed this place over in the past because they don't have shish kebab. But a friend recommended it and I gave it a try yesterday.\n\nMy choice was the beef shawarma plate which came with a salad, hummus, pita bread and some pickles.\n\nThe beef was excellent quality without the usual fat and gristle too many shawarma places give you. It had been marinated in a delicious sauce. The hummus was also flavorful. I was recently in the middle east and this definitely had the authentic flavors.\n\nThe $9 price was also a good deal for someone like me who does not need huge portions.\n\nIf they added lamb shish kebab to the menu I would happily give it five stars! In Isla Vista a bicycle rack would also be nice! Please give this place a try!"}]}
