{'name': 'Mels', 'address': '209 W Carrillo St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Beer, Wine & Spirits, Bars, Food, Nightlife, Karaoke, Dive Bars', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': True, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': True, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-08-26 22:47:42', 'review_text': "Divey but charming little spot. \n\nMel's has been a fixture of the Santa Barbara community for probably 60 years. It's a no-nonsense setting good for a heavy pour. The current location doesn't have the same level of nostalgia that the original spot next to the Paseo Nuevo movie theater did, but it's a lot larger with a hidden few seating rooms on the western side of the venue. Parking is nearly non-existent with the small area currently being used as a parklet, but you shouldn't be drinking and driving anyway! Take an Uber!\n\nI've been when there's a crowd but prefer coming on a quieter evening mid-week. For being on an extremely busy corner, I'm in awe over just how small-town the interior feels. The service is very personal which I appreciate. I've been served by Jennifer, the bartender, and feel that she does a great job. \n\nI was here the other night and happened to walk into a small, impromptu stand-up comedy show. I didn't expect to be entertained but it was a fun time nonetheless!\n\nMel's may seem like a drive-by, but stop by and see just how special of a spot it really is."}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2020-08-02 01:26:34', 'review_text': 'Little local spot. Decent beer. Pool table so time too. Fun during comedy nights. Managements seems a little unprofessional at times. But aside from that decent local little bar'}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2020-03-06 00:46:21', 'review_text': "Mel's has evolved into a Mexican bar. Be prepared for mariachi on the juke box! Nice bartender!"}]}
