the time).\nThat location did suffer from being inconsistent but ultimately we liked the spot.\n\nThe other day, their Banzai burrito popped into my head and I had to have one.  Now living back in Santa Barbara, I enlisted a friend of mine who is UCSB alum to help me navigate the incredible bureaucracy that is even finding a place to park and paying for it, then walking the four miles to the Wahoo's location.\n\nI of course had the glorious banzai burrito: the asada was tender, the green sauce was green....it was nicely hot inside and out and delicious.  I believe that they do use microwaves which isnt ideal but this burrito was as good as I remember any of them being for the many years that I got them in LA!\n\nMy buddy had the chicken sandwich and he really like it as well.\n\nI will be back!!"}]}
