tered about, and time seems to float by as you hang out in a place that would be cool in any era of history, from past to future. \n\nIt's worth the uber ride, and once you're out here, hit up the imperial. Same owners, same vibe, bigger patio. Both are great."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-04-15 00:47:59', 'review_text': "We are big, big fans of The Merc. They have great art for sale, pop-ups, trivia nights, bands, movie nights, you name it, they do it!! \n\nOh and they also have awesome beer! They've always got something new and local on tap. They switch it up pretty frequently too. But don't worry, The Merc keeps our favorites on the shelf so we always know we'll have a winner at every visit. \n\nRecently, we went in during the quarantine. They'd been closed, but posted on facebook that they'd be open for a couple of hours for bottles to go. We hustled over to pick up some delicious beers we can't get in stores as well as some awesome hoodie sweaters!"}]}
