arking lot. Today wasn't going to be the day either, but when we found that the sushi spot we wanted to hit was closed, we pivoted to Kanaloa. I'm here to tell you that it was a great choice.\n\nI had the grilled fish sandwich and fresh chips. My wife and daughter got poke bowls. It was all extremely fresh and delicious. I'd do it again in a heartbeat. In addition, the service was very friendly and helpful, ordering was a breeze, there was plenty of seating, and the food came out quickly and perfectly done. I'm not sure it's always this awesome, but I simply don't care. I will be back."}]}
