{'name': 'The Coffee Bean & Tea Leaf', 'address': '3052 De La Vina', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Food, Coffee & Tea, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '6:0-18:0', 'Tuesday': '6:0-18:0', 'Wednesday': '6:0-18:0', 'Thursday': '6:0-18:0', 'Friday': '6:0-18:0', 'Saturday': '6:0-18:0', 'Sunday': '6:0-18:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2020-02-01 01:45:04', 'review_text': 'My gripe with my experience would pertain to the rudeness of the wait staff and the lack of care towards their customer. I find it absurd that that they have the audacity to charge for a cup after their cup failed to preform. Please fulfill your coffee needs elsewhere.'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2020-01-13 15:31:02', 'review_text': "Well, if you're in a hurry and, say, order ahead of time like I do, leave extra time for a lecture from the staff if they don't like the way you ordered your drink. My drink was withheld. I was held up in the morning by an employee. She wasn't friendly or accommodating. It wasn't as if I was patronizing their business. I was essentially scolded with no respect for my time or the fact that I purchase things here often. This isn't the first time. We were treated rudely about refills on more than one occasion with the staff demanding a receipt (even when they never gave us one). I don't need the third degree or rude treatment when I'm overpaying for coffee on a Monday morning. I suggest going to the State Street location where the staff is always friendly, accommodating, and wonderful."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2020-01-06 01:40:12', 'review_text': "Nice shaded location (near TJ's) and there is almost always a parking space. One of the few coffee shops around town that has power outlets. Solid coffee. Decent Jasmine and Dragonwell green tea. $1.00 refill for coffee. The service is great for the most part - it seems like quite a few people work here. However, the employee this morning left a bad taste in my mouth. She didn't say anything specifically unkind, but I got the feeling my presence was a burden to her. Maybe she is in pain and doesn't have much kindness to give. I've worked many years in retail - and I know workers aren't robots and have complex inner lives - but even at my worst I could fake it, or at least not be a grouch to my customers. I left feeling a bit resentful (or hurt) that a stranger would be so rigid and unkind to me. I don't deserve that! I'll get over it though haha. For prospective customers: the organic light roast (Peru) was infinitely better than the dark roast, which I had for refill. Four stars because of the location, affordability, power outlets, and most of the customer service. I couldn't go full 5 stars because, frankly, it's 2020 and you can find tastier, more complex, higher-quality coffee elsewhere."}]}
