n the menu, and when the roll did not come with cream cheese I asked our server if it was possible for me to have a side of it with my meal. He proceeded to ask me if I was certain I had ordered my roll with cream cheese, and when I said I thought so he disagreed with me and told me that he "had a pretty good memory". Flustered I said that I was fine and didn\'t need any, and he eventually said "well if that\'s what you want" and left. I am so disappointed in Kyoto sushi because I have been here before and so enjoy the delicious menu items every time I go, but after this encounter I will not be coming back. Given that there was an automatic gratuity for the tip, there was no way for our party to express our distaste in the rudeness of our server. Working in food service myself, I know the job can be tiring and difficult, and I really try to understand the perspective of the worker. But my party did absolutely nothing wrong, and I personally would never have treated a customer in the rude way we were treated.'}]}
