ally is ABOUT THE WINE:  \n\nIn an area such as the Santa Barbara waterfront, where wine offerings are a plenty, make time to stop at Les Marchands.   This wine bar goes beyond a tasting room and is as good as it gets if you\'re looking for one stop offering of impeccable service, knowledgable staff, gracious hospitality, outdoor patio, and a wine list that represents the California footprint with expertise.  \n\nFood pairings are a delight when reading up on their menu, you\'ll be excited to read the names of many hard to find, stunning wines from local family owned, small production vitners as a common offering at this wine bar, i.e. Bryan Babcock\'s "Ocean\'s Ghost" Pinot Noir (a 92 point effort on the 2016 bottling).  \n\nThe only crime is that I live so far away and can only enjoy when I return home to California!'}]}
