{'name': 'Paseo Nuevo Shopping Center', 'address': '651 Paseo Nuevo', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'American (Traditional), Restaurants, Shopping Centers, Shopping, Local Flavor', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '11:0-19:0', 'Wednesday': '11:0-19:0', 'Thursday': '11:0-19:0', 'Friday': '9:0-17:0', 'Saturday': '11:0-19:0', 'Sunday': '11:0-19:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': True, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-12 01:33:55', 'review_text': 'Paseo Nuevo is one of the few malls in America that has successfully managed to stay afloat after all these years. \n\nThis outdoor mall feels very authentic and gives off an non-commercialized "Santa Barbara" vibe even though there are a good amount of chain stores here. Even with the steady decline of the American shopping mall, Paseo Nuevo sure can hold its own. \n\nThe mall received a high-budget refresh and looks great. I feel that although the before version was just fine, a fresh coat of paint and new paver pathways (among other enhancements) really brought this place into the current decade. \n\nNo matter which corner of Paseo Nuevo you happen to be at, you\'re sure to be in for a treat. The mall is adorned with beautiful plants and ornate ironwork, and I feel that most every shop is occupied which is a welcome change to vacant State Street. You\'ll find all types of small boutiques and little cafes here for your enjoyment. While the two anchor retail stores no longer occupy the mall, there\'s talk that one of them will be transitioning to a roller rink which I look forward to seeing. \n\nA great plaza overall. The American mall is not dead!'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-09 03:33:11', 'review_text': 'Everything closes at 7pm?! Everyday. Even weekends. Tried to do some shopping after work but nope. Amazon it is I guess.  No wonder none of the businesses make it.'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-07-11 22:34:28', 'review_text': "Don't park your bike in the garage! One of our bikes got stolen here! Security was no help. There's no cameras in the garage either."}]}
