{'name': "Gino's Sicilian Express", 'address': '12 W Figueroa St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Italian, Salad, Pizza, Restaurants, Sandwiches', 'hours': {'Monday': '11:30-21:0', 'Tuesday': '11:30-21:0', 'Wednesday': '11:30-21:0', 'Thursday': '11:30-21:0', 'Friday': '11:30-21:0', 'Saturday': '11:30-21:0', 'Sunday': '13:0-20:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': False, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': None, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-26 01:06:59', 'review_text': 'Told you I would be back..\nWhat I didn\'t tell you was\nI\'m coming back the same week..\nChristmas Eve, me being late to make food choices.\nI called to see if Ginos was open..\nScore!\nThey were.\n\nI tried the "Chicken Pesto panini "\nThey told me I got the last sandwich bread used to make it.\nNot sure if me getting the last one was worthy of a medallion.\nBut hey, I enjoyed the sandwich \nAnd I can see I will be back to taste it again\nNext time I seek to be the first to get the sandwich bread\nThe taste of the pesto was good, above average.\n\nHere are some things that would have made this sandwich better.\nAsk for more pesto ( I liked the flavor)\nAsk if the chicken can be cut into smaller pieces \n( definitely real chicken breast, it was a little on the dry side)\nI don\'t mind that. But most will.\nThat\'s it....\nI recommend others to try it..\nWould like to know what they think \nCustomer service was excellent.\nGave the feeling I was dealing with mom and pop\nAnd not a corporate automated strategy'}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-23 01:59:25', 'review_text': "Pizza by the slice\nWith a full menu of choices\nI had the opportunity to try this place \nRecently \nAnd here is my thoughts \n\nCustomer service, okay... no issues\nI sat inside since outside was on the cool side\nNot to mention it was the day for cleaning trucks \nTo make their appearance \n\nHad a nostalgic feel to it\nNoticing the inside decor.\nOnly thing missing was the mobsters..\n\nFood wise...\nI'm going to look at this review with a different perspective \nWe will incorporate price.\nFor the price that is offered,  3.50 per slice.\nIt's going to be hard to beat this place\nIf you are on a budget, looking for pizza\nWithout the extra amount...( a whole pie)\nThey do a good deal\nYou get up to three ingredients too\n\nConsidering taste..\nIt's pizza ladies and gentlemen.\nI wasn't disappointed \nNor did I find my taste buds sending signals to the moon\nI simply sat in my chair enjoying the pics on the wall\nAlong with the grey Santa Barbara afternoon.\nI got pepperoni, sausage and olives as my three choices\n\n\n\nI didn't find the ingredients to be authentic \nThe sausage was okay, ( better if browned by itself and added)\npepperoni standard, \nolives canned\nBut what they do have they utilize well \nI still have more items to try\n\n\nThe location is as prime as it gets...\nSmack in the heart of downtown \n\nI will say,\nWhile sitting down eating \nI noticed different populations of people \nComing in to order\nI payed attention to how they were treated \nAnd watched as they got their orders to sit or walk away \nEveryone was happy, \nDecompressing over the hustle and bustle \nrooted in the holiday season\nWhile seated inside, we all ate as one family\nUntil the last bite..\n\nI will be back."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-18 20:11:38', 'review_text': "BEST NY style pizza.\n\n\n\n....Gino's is a tiny cubbyhole on Figueroa st and serves excellent NY style pizza by the pie or slice\nthe combination of sauce , cheese,crust and toppings are a delight to the senses and friendly fast service is the time.The whole pies have names of Monsters ...my favorite is the Gotti.Treat yourself and visit this outstanding pizzaria\n!!!!"}]}
