ing drinks for his friend that was hanging out by the game table (i think kyle was his name ?) and gave him free oreo slush smoothies without lids. i waited for 15 minutes before he actually acknowledged i was a paying customer, after we made contact several times and i\'d rang the little metal bell (to which he responded with a glare and condescendingly scoffed "yes.......?" before looking away and going back to ignoring me). when he finally decided i was worthy of his attention, he stared at me and tried to argue with me that he didn\'t mess up my order. i had to pull up my most recent order and previous orders as proof, and even then he did not admit any mistake or apologize. when i asked if he could remake my drink as ordered, he was clearly unhappy and showed it by making the drink as slow as he could and once again incorrectly. by that time i\'d already been there for an extra 30 mins and didn\'t have any more time to waste, so i said thank you apologized for the inconvenience and said goodbye. however this was the worst boba experience i\'ve yet to experience, i don\'t wish it on anyone else, and will not ever subject myself to such a waste of time and money again :('}]}
