he responded that they were out of the catfish, so I  ordered the Red Snapper fillet. She informed me that that night the red snapper was actually the whole fish, not just the fillet. I said I would try it. Our food arrived and my friend really enjoyed her meal, but I picked at the fish and unfortunately got some bones in my mouth. It didn't taste like much and it came with plain rice."}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-26 03:10:29', 'review_text': "OK so I'm writing this review almost 2 hours after we entered the restaurant. We were here for Thanksgiving when they had a 5 course vegan meal for $65. So far we got just 2 and they were pretty good to be honest. But here I'm shivering in the cold, because they do no know how to fix the outdoor heater(there are few other people equally frustrated as me) . The service is chaotic, there is only one woman who knew what was going around. To summarize\n1) really bad service\n2)\xa0 the food is good but without coherent staff you cannot have a good experience dining here. \n\nI'd avoid this place if I read the last few reviews. Too late for me, I hope I get my next course before the Turkish delight store next door closes (at 8)\n\nWe finally got our food and we were out by 8 pm, thanks to Julie who was our only saving grace."}]}
