{'name': 'Piranha Restaurant & Sushi Bar', 'address': '714 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Sushi Bars', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 3.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2008-08-08 19:51:46', 'review_text': 'The sushi was mediocre but I still like the environment and the service!'}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2008-07-26 05:03:21', 'review_text': '"after a lovely day at the beach, my husband and i decided to finish off the day with some sushi. we\'d eaten at piranha before and enjoyed it, but after tonight\'s experience, i can safely say we will never return. it wasn\'t heinous--but for 80$, the quality of the food and service was pretty abysmal. not only was the sushi NOT super fresh and tasty, especially as compared to katsuya in encino, but the waitstaff was inattentive (we had to call out for the hostess finally to get our waitress\'s attention), the waitress made a mistake on our order and did not recitfy it (she brought out sea urchin instead of eel--when we brought it to her attention, she did not remove the unwanted, uneaten item from our bill), AND there was a long hair in one of our rolls! At most sushi establishments, they bring out the items as they are prepared, but here, we had to wait a fairly long time before  being served, and then it was everything, all at once.  Plus, i really like it when the meal commences with a nice, warm hand towel and some complimentary edaname--typical of most sushi places, but NOT here. Overall, a very unpleasant, unappetizing, unsatisfying gastronomical experience!"'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2008-06-02 15:01:40', 'review_text': "This is a nice 