 next door at Panino and had a great sandwich."}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2016-03-11 23:01:38', 'review_text': "Came here for breakfast/brunch with friends. They have a wide variety of foods to choose from, so there's probably something for everyone.\n\nI love the Papas Santa Barbara!! The potatoes are nice and crispy, and topped with cheese, avocado, tomato, and chicken bits you can't go wrong. But I think it could've used more salsa or something, and it's a little expensive considering it's mostly potatoes but that's how breakfast foods are typically.\n\nTheir shaved snow dessert was decent! I tried the oriental flavor that has this soybean powder stuff on top (kinako in Japanese) that's so bomb!! I love kinako so it was cool to find a place around SB that uses it. It also has crunchy little cereal bits that add nice texture.\n\nMy friend got the bulgogi burrito I think. They flavor was okay, but it wasn't very impressive to me and I personally wouldn't order it again.\n\nThe workers were really nice! Half of my group got backyard bowls but they still let us all sit inside the restaurant :)"}]}
