{'name': 'La Salsa', 'address': '3938 State St, Ste 200', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Salad, Mexican, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '10:0-21:0', 'Tuesday': '10:0-21:0', 'Wednesday': '10:0-21:0', 'Thursday': '10:0-21:0', 'Friday': '10:0-21:0', 'Saturday': '10:30-21:0', 'Sunday': '11:0-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2017-11-19 22:33:41', 'review_text': "The salsa bar looks really fresh with reasonable pricing. I see that they're grilling the chicken on the spot and makes me look forward to my order"}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2017-08-20 22:57:43', 'review_text': "First off:  Don't eat here.\n\nSecond off:  Don't eat here. \n\nOK, so basically I just needed a quick lunch and I'm always down for a taco.  Hadn't been to a La Salsa in FOREVER, so this was a good plan (or so I thought).  I walked in and it was pretty busy, but by the time I placed my order it had cleared out.  I decided to get a Kids' Meal Quesadilla with black beans.\n\nAll in all things were fine with my meal; it was served hot so good so far.  (The only reason this review isn't 1 STAR is because their Mango Salsa.)  My soda tasted good, the chips were fine enough.  I began to eat my meal as I was sitting in one of the booths near the front door.\n\nAnother employee comes to the front door (near me) and starts spraying Windex and begins to clean the window.  I DO NOT want WINDEX in my food!  Then, she gets a broom and starts to sweep (no lie).  Then, gets out her mop and bucket and MOPS THE FLOOR.\n\nThis place is pretty small, so I could have given them a pass if she had mopped on the other side of the store, or oh, I DON'T KNOW WHEN THERE WERE NOT ANY CUSTOMERS around!?\n\nPretty gross.  Then, to top it off the employees started to BLAST the music so loud I didn't finish my basic queso.  \n\nNah, skip this place."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2017-08-05 22:37:00', 'review_text': "One of the FAVES to stop and eat when driving through Santa Barbara.  Why?\n\n1.   It's fresh Mexican food made to order.\n2.  Authentic style without grease\n3.  Simple and easy to eat\n4.  The salsa bar is small but diverse\n5.  Great prices\n6. Great location off the 101/154\n7.  It's consistent!\n\nSo, definitely try it out.  Ignore the naysayers.\nTry the Mexico City tacos!\nTry the nachos.  They're HUGE!\nTry the mango salsa too.\n\nEnjoy!  You'll be back!!"}]}
