{'name': 'Billies', 'address': '413 State St, Cross St Gutierrez', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Bars, Local Flavor, Diners, Nightlife, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '10:0-3:0', 'Tuesday': '10:0-3:0', 'Wednesday': '10:0-3:0', 'Thursday': '10:0-3:0', 'Friday': '10:0-3:0', 'Saturday': '10:0-3:0', 'Sunday': '10:0-3:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': False, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2011-05-22 19:01:42', 'review_text': 'New ownership, now called Mamma Donna.\nWas good before, -much, much better now!'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2011-01-09 23:43:35', 'review_text': "A Star Trek Pinball machine?!!?!?!?!!? Count me in!!!!!\n\nThe last night of school this past semester my friends and I had a nice long party in downtown Santa Barbara. Once the bars were closed and we were thoroughly famished we decided to go to Billies. I had walked by it MANY times and it always smelt great but never took the time to go in.\n\nThe first thing to understand about going to Billies during the post-bar period is it's one of a select few restaurants that are open until very early so it will literally be swamped with people, most of whom are too drunk to put three sensical words together.\n\nThe night I was there there had been a scheduling error and they were understaffed. With a line out the door there was only one person working the counter and one cook. Watching this man work his heart out and still have a positive attitude I gained a real respect for him. If I were in his place I'd be hanging myself in the back room.\n\nWe finally got to order and I was told by multiple people that the Mac and Cheese is iconic.\n\nFood Tip: The Mac and Cheese is iconic.\n\nIt was priced decently and there are unlimited fountain drinks (which was fantastic) and while I was waiting for my order I geeked it up on the Star Trek pinball machine. Most of my friends were passed out in a booth and I was a light drinker that night so I had plenty of energy. \n\nOnce the food came I discovered that portions are not something they care about at Billies. It was a massive bowl of Mac and Cheese for just a couple of bucks. I enjoyed the food do a long while, then shared it with some friends. There was plenty to go around.\n\nBy the time we left it had calmed down a little. I thanked the man behind the counter for being so nice and working so hard and told him I would recommend Billies to everyone I know. That being said, here ya go everyone!"}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2010-12-13 23:25:14', 'review_text': "I haven't tried any of the food, but my friend's friend works here and we decided to drop by, actually i always drop by whenever i'm in the sb area. this bar isn't as busy as the other bars, but i guess if you just want a good beer and watch tv it's a good place. my friend also told me that they open til 3 while all the others close at 2am. \n\ngood for happy hour!"}]}
