{'name': 'Nutbelly Pizzeria and Deli', 'address': '915 Linden Ave', 'city': 'Carpinteria', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Delis, Sandwiches, Italian, Pizza, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '11:0-21:0', 'Wednesday': '11:0-21:0', 'Thursday': '11:0-21:0', 'Friday': '11:0-21:0', 'Saturday': '11:0-21:0', 'Sunday': '11:0-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': None, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': None, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-14 18:31:01', 'review_text': "This turned out to be a really great place to hang out and eat pizza while waiting for our train.  Really good food and great service! And I don't drink wine,  but the two people I was with said that the wine choices were excellent.  Will definitely return on our next visit to town."}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-30 03:50:16', 'review_text': "Totally love the food but staff could be more sensitive to keeping the genre of music played in line with the ambience of the restaurant.  Cultural appropriation not withstanding,  a pizza restaurant should not feel as if one is in a Mexican restaurant unless it's in Mexico (which, of course,  at that point,  would be understandable ).  The beauty of living in a multi-cultural country is that allows us to culture shop between various ambiences.  If I want to go to a Latino restaurant,  I will choose that and enjoy it whole-heartedly- bring on the Salas,  Banderia and Bachata!  If I want to go to a Chinese restaurant,  I will go there to experience that culture and ambience. If I want Italian American or Californian pizzeria, please let me have it.  Confusing things between cultures kills your business which us why the restaurant was empty despite having good food, good beer on tap and sportsball on TV...."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-29 21:47:14', 'review_text': "Came here for lunch with a large group of 12 people. Everyone working here was so nice and accommodating. The service was fantastic. The food was fantastic, love that they offered vegan options. Very kid friendly. Love the outdoor seating. Can't wait to go back. Would absolutely recommend this place!"}]}
