can grab a ticket at the booth and drive right onto the wharf. First 90 minutes of parking are free.\n\n-If you do drive go slowly, it sounds and feels like riding a wooden rollercoaster in slow-motion and you are driving on old wood and metal bolts.\n\n-Fishing is allowed at the end of the wharf and you'll see crab traps and fishing happening which is fun for the kids.\n\n-There are free public bathrooms.\n\n-Not much to see and do unless you have dinner plans, hilariously we saw staff rounding up wayward outdoor-seating customers that ran off to take pictures. The concern was seagulls would eat their unguarded food.\n\n-There is a psychic/fortune teller on the pier, super nostalgic though they were closed when we went."}]}
