rs who were seated further down, and frankly, seemed to get more attention. Three scallops, mashed potato's and asparagus for $45 seems a bit overpriced even in this area and at that service level is a really disappointing. We finally asked for the bill so we could get up and leave."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-09 23:47:16', 'review_text': 'Spectularly beautiful, feels mediterrean .... we were totally geared up to love it. The bread serve with nicely creamy butter with Hawaiian salt on top is super nice. I do have to say that the salmon was served with sauce, sauce, sauce, sauce and sauce. It detracted from experiencing the wonder of the fish itself. It was rich and maybe I eat too lean most of the time because it almost was nauseatingly rich. I wanted to love everything about this place and I do plan to return and voyage into other menu items carefully making sure I cover how rich the dish is and how saucey. The waiter was great, not intrusive. I have to give them another try.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-09 00:57:48', 'review_text': "Absolutely delicious and great restaurant. Service was outstanding and quick. Came here for my fiancé's birthday. We dinned outside and it was perfect and hope if we are ever back in the area that we come here again. It's a little pricey but worth every dollar. I ordered the gnocchi and my fiancé had the black ink spaghetti. We also ordered calamari. Each one of these dishes were delicious and portions are a good size!"}]}
